      "text": "Sandalwood; imported by Solomon from Ophir for the temple, for his own house, and for musical instruments, 1 Kgs. 10:11–12; 2 Chr. 2:8; 9:10–11. The wood used was probably the red sandalwood of India, of which musical instruments are still made.",
